# Every global athanor-compositor can offer, and who receives it (doc_own_stack.md OS4, OS5).
# One row per global, `<interface> <class>`; `#` starts a comment line. The classes:
#   standard     offered to every client
#   unconfined   offered to every client outside a security context
#   layer-gated  offered to every client; its top and overlay layers are refused unless the
#                allow-list grants them (`State::layer_commit`)
#   privileged   offered only to the clients the allow-list grants it, never inside a security
#                context
# The privileged and layer-gated rows are the interfaces the allow-list may name
# (data/privileged-clients). The fixture fails on an offered global without a row
# (os9_every_global_is_classified).
wl_compositor standard
wl_subcompositor standard
wl_shm standard
wl_seat standard
wl_output standard
xdg_wm_base standard
zxdg_output_manager_v1 standard
wp_viewporter standard
wp_single_pixel_buffer_manager_v1 standard
wp_fractional_scale_manager_v1 standard
wp_presentation standard
wp_cursor_shape_manager_v1 standard
xdg_activation_v1 standard
wl_data_device_manager standard
ext_idle_notifier_v1 standard
# On a render node only, and linux-drm-syncobj-v1 only on one that can wait on a syncobj.
zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 standard
wp_linux_drm_syncobj_manager_v1 standard
wp_security_context_manager_v1 unconfined
zwp_text_input_manager_v3 unconfined
zwlr_layer_shell_v1 layer-gated
ext_foreign_toplevel_list_v1 privileged
ext_foreign_toplevel_image_capture_source_manager_v1 privileged
ext_output_image_capture_source_manager_v1 privileged
